
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G H : Points
A,B,D are collinear [00]
CD ⟂ AB [01]
A,C,E are collinear [02]
BE ⟂ AC [03]
FA = FB [04]
FB = FC [05]
FG = FC [06]
D,C,G are collinear [07]
B,E,H are collinear [08]
D,H,C are collinear [09]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. FA = FB [04] & FB = FC [05] & FG = FC [06] ⇒  A,B,C,G are concyclic [10]
002. A,B,C,G are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠ABC = ∠AGC [11]
003. A,B,C,G are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠ABG = ∠ACG [12]
004. A,C,E are collinear [02] & A,B,D are collinear [00] & CD ⟂ AB [01] & BE ⟂ AC [03] ⇒  ∠CEB = ∠CDB [13]
005. ∠CEB = ∠CDB [13] ⇒  D,B,C,E are concyclic [14]
006. D,B,C,E are concyclic [14] ⇒  ∠BCD = ∠BED [15]
007. A,C,E are collinear [02] & H,E,B are collinear [08] & A,B,D are collinear [00] & H,D,C are collinear [09] & CD ⟂ AB [01] & BE ⟂ AC [03] ⇒  ∠AEH = ∠ADH [16]
008. ∠AEH = ∠ADH [16] ⇒  A,H,D,E are concyclic [17]
009. A,H,D,E are concyclic [17] ⇒  ∠AHE = ∠ADE [18]
010. A,B,D are collinear [00] & ∠ABC = ∠AGC [11] & D,C,G are collinear [07] & ∠BCD = ∠BED [15] & ∠AHE = ∠ADE [18] & B,E,H are collinear [08] ⇒  ∠HAD = ∠DAG [19]
011. D,C,G are collinear [07] & D,H,C are collinear [09] ⇒  D,H,G are collinear [20]
012. ∠HAD = ∠DAG [19] & D,H,G are collinear [20] ⇒  DH:DG = AH:AG [21]
013. A,B,D are collinear [00] & H,D,C are collinear [09] & G,C,D are collinear [07] & CD ⟂ AB [01] ⇒  ∠BDH = ∠GDB [22]
014. H,D,C are collinear [09] & CD ⟂ AB [01] ⇒  DH ⟂ AB [23]
015. DH ⟂ AB [23] & BE ⟂ AC [03] ⇒  ∠(DH-BE) = ∠BAC [24]
016. B,H,E are collinear [08] & D,C,H are collinear [09] & D,C,G are collinear [07] & ∠ABG = ∠ACG [12] & ∠(DH-BE) = ∠BAC [24] ⇒  ∠BHD = ∠DGB [25]
017. ∠BDH = ∠GDB [22] & ∠BHD = ∠DGB [25] (Similar Triangles)⇒  DH = DG [26]
018. DH:DG = AH:AG [21] & DH = DG [26] ⇒  AH = AG
==========================
